vncviewer only has X11 code (XKB, XInput, Surface_X11) and dereferences
fl_display right after fl_open_display(). The Termux fltk is built with
--enable-wayland, so when WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set FLTK picks its Wayland
backend, fl_display stays NULL and vncviewer segfaults. Force the X11
backend (Xwayland on Wayland sessions).

--- a/vncviewer/vncviewer.cxx
+++ b/vncviewer/vncviewer.cxx
@@ -723,6 +723,9 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv)
   }
 
 #if !defined(WIN32) && !defined(__APPLE__)
+  // FLTK 1.4 is a Wayland/X11 hybrid, but this viewer is X11 only.
+  setenv("FLTK_BACKEND", "x11", 1);
+
   if (strcmp(display, "") != 0) {
     Fl::display(display);
   }
